=== Summary (2023-05-31 -> 2026-05-08) ===
  Observations:        518 across 14 tickers, 37 months
  Cross-sectional IC:  mean=-0.034  std=0.309  t=-0.66
  Annualized IR:       -0.38
  Pooled IC:           +0.010
  Hit rate (long):     56% over 283 long signals
  Hit rate (short):    46% over 235 short signals
  Quintile fwd rets:   Q1=+3.19% · Q2=+2.96% · Q3=+2.00% · Q4=+3.98% · Q5=+0.88%
  L-S per rebalance:   +0.31% mean, +11.63% summed

=== Plain-English ===
  [overview] Backbone Quant Score backtest: 518 (ticker × month) observations across 14 tickers and 37 months (2023-05-31 → 2026-05-08). Forward window: 21 trading days.

  [skill] Monthly cross-sectional IC: mean -0.034, std 0.309, t-stat -0.66. Annualized IR: -0.38 — negative — the score points the wrong way over this window. Pooled IC across all observations: +0.010. Interpretation: the cross-sectional rank correlation is negative on average — the score is mis-ordering names in this sample.

  [hits] Hit rates conditioned on signal direction: long signals (n=283) closed positive 56% of the time; short signals (n=235) closed negative 46% of the time. 50% would mean the signal adds no edge over a coin flip.

  [quintiles] Mean forward return by score quintile (Q1=lowest score → Q5=highest): Q1=+3.19% (n=104), Q2=+2.96% (n=103), Q3=+2.00% (n=104), Q4=+3.98% (n=103), Q5=+0.88% (n=104)

  [portfolio] Equal-weight long-top-quintile / short-bottom-quintile portfolio, rebalanced every 21 trading days: mean per-period return +0.31%, summed across the window +11.63%. This is a simple sum, not a compounded total — it isolates the per-rebalance edge before transaction costs, financing, and slippage.

  [caveats] Caveats: (1) This is a 'backbone' backtest — it covers ~65% of the Quant Score by weight (technical, regime, statistics, spectral, topology). Peer/valuation, sentiment, and risk_framework are excluded because yfinance cannot supply them point-in-time without lookahead bias. (2) Costs, slippage, and short-borrow are ignored. (3) The watchlist is a single sector cluster, so the cross-section is small — IR estimates are noisy.

=== Excluded (would inject lookahead on yfinance) ===
  valuation: needs point-in-time peer multiples (paid data feed required)
  sentiment: yfinance only returns recent news; no historical archive
  risk: risk_framework fetches its own data; not sliceable to a cutoff
